var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"cycles/#Survey-cycles-and-table-names","page":"Survey cycles and table names","text":"Continuous NHANES runs in two-year cycles. A table name is a base name plus a cycle marker, so the same measurement carries a different name in each cycle: demographics is DEMO for 1999-2000 and DEMO_J for 2017-2018.\n\nYears Marker Example\n1999-2000 (none) DEMO\n2001-2002 _B DEMO_B\n2003-2004 _C DEMO_C\n2005-2006 _D DEMO_D\n2007-2008 _E DEMO_E\n2009-2010 _F DEMO_F\n2011-2012 _G DEMO_G\n2013-2014 _H DEMO_H\n2015-2016 _I DEMO_I\n2017-2018 _J DEMO_J\n2017-March 2020 P_ prefix P_DEMO\n2021-2023 _L DEMO_L\n\njulia> NHANES.survey_years()\n11-element Vector{Int64}:\n 1999\n 2001\n 2003\n 2005\n 2007\n 2009\n 2011\n 2013\n 2015\n 2017\n 2021","title":"Survey cycles and table names"},{"category":"section","location":"cycles/#Years-and-markers","page":"Survey cycles and table names","text":"NHANES.cycle_suffix maps a cycle start year to its marker, and NHANES.suffix_to_year maps back. suffix_to_year accepts the marker with or without its underscore.\n\njulia> NHANES.cycle_suffix(2017)\n\"_J\"\n\njulia> NHANES.cycle_suffix(1999)\n\"\"\n\njulia> NHANES.suffix_to_year(\"_J\")\n2017\n\njulia> NHANES.suffix_to_year(\"B\")\n2001","title":"Years and markers"},{"category":"section","location":"cycles/#The-missing-2019-2020-cycle","page":"Survey cycles and table names","text":"COVID-19 cut the 2019-2020 collection short. CDC folded the partial data into the 2017-March 2020 pre-pandemic files, which use a P_ prefix rather than a suffix, and skipped the letter _K, so 2021-2023 is _L. Asking for 2019 says so.\n\njulia> NHANES.cycle_suffix(2019)\nERROR: ArgumentError: NHANES 2019-2020 was never released publicly: data collection was cut short by COVID-19 and the results were folded into the 2017-March 2020 pre-pandemic files. Use the pre-pandemic cycle :P instead.\n\nPass the symbol :P where a year is expected to reach the pre-pandemic cycle.\n\nNHANES.tables(:Examination, :P)\nNHANES.download(\"P_BMX\")","title":"The missing 2019-2020 cycle"},{"category":"section","location":"cycles/#Splitting-a-table-name","page":"Survey cycles and table names","text":"NHANES.parse_table_name separates the base name from the cycle marker. A base name may itself contain underscores, so only a trailing single letter that is a known marker counts as a suffix.\n\njulia> NHANES.parse_table_name(\"DEMO_J\")\n(\"DEMO\", \"_J\")\n\njulia> NHANES.parse_table_name(\"ALB_CR_J\")\n(\"ALB_CR\", \"_J\")\n\njulia> NHANES.parse_table_name(\"P_BMX\")\n(\"BMX\", \"P_\")\n\njulia> NHANES.parse_table_name(\"DEMO\")\n(\"DEMO\", \"\")","title":"Splitting a table name"},{"category":"section","location":"cycles/#Components","page":"Survey cycles and table names","text":"Five components partition the survey. Each accepts its full name or its R-style short name, in any case.\n\njulia> NHANES.COMPONENTS\n(:Demographics, :Dietary, :Examination, :Laboratory, :Questionnaire)\n\njulia> NHANES.normalize_component(:LAB)\n:Laboratory\n\njulia> NHANES.normalize_component(:demographics)\n:Demographics","title":"Components"},{"category":"section","location":"cycles/#URLs","page":"Survey cycles and table names","text":"The URL for a table follows from its marker: the cycle start year names the directory, and pre-pandemic tables live in the 2017 directory alongside the 2017-2018 files.\n\njulia> NHANES.table_url(\"DEMO_J\")\n\"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Data/Nhanes/Public/2017/DataFiles/DEMO_J.xpt\"\n\njulia> NHANES.table_url(\"P_BMX\")\n\"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Data/Nhanes/Public/2017/DataFiles/P_BMX.xpt\"\n\njulia> NHANES.codebook_url(\"BMX_D\")\n\"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Data/Nhanes/Public/2005/DataFiles/BMX_D.htm\"\n\njulia> NHANES.variablelist_url(:Laboratory, 2015)\n\"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/nchs/nhanes/search/variablelist.aspx?Component=Laboratory&CycleBeginYear=2015\"\n\njulia> NHANES.variablelist_url(:Examination, :P)\n\"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/nchs/nhanes/search/variablelist.aspx?Component=Examination&Cycle=2017-2020\"\n\nListing pages link to their data files relatively, so NHANES.resolve_url resolves a link against the page it came from.\n\njulia> NHANES.resolve_url(\n           \"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/nchs/nhanes/nhanes3/datafiles.aspx\",\n           \"../../data/nhanes3/1a/adult.dat\",\n       )\n\"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/nchs/data/nhanes3/1a/adult.dat\"","title":"URLs"},{"category":"section","location":"cycles/#DXA-cycles","page":"Survey cycles and table names","text":"Dual energy X-ray absorptiometry data covers four cycles and sits outside the component listings, so NHANES.dxa_tables builds its names and URLs directly.\n\njulia> NHANES.DXA_YEARS\n(1999, 2001, 2003, 2005)\n\njulia> NHANES.dxa_tables(2005).name\n1-element Vector{String}:\n \"DXX_D\"\n\njulia> NHANES.dxa_tables(2005; suppl = true).url\n1-element Vector{String}:\n \"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Data/Nhanes/Public/2005/DataFiles/dxx_d_s.xpt\"\n\nDownloading the data itself needs the network.\n\nNHANES.dxa(2005)\nNHANES.dxa(2005; suppl = true)","title":"DXA cycles"},{"category":"section","location":"cycles/#Historical-surveys","page":"Survey cycles and table names","text":"The three surveys that predate continuous NHANES are named rather than dated.\n\njulia> NHANES.HISTORICAL_SURVEYS\n(:nhanes1, :nhanes2, :nhanes3)\n\nTheir listings carry an absolute url per file, since the names do not follow the continuous cycle scheme.\n\nNHANES.historical_tables(:nhanes3)\ndf = NHANES.historical_download(:nhanes3, \"SSNH3MGM\")\npath = NHANES.historical_file(:nhanes1, \"DU4111\")\n\nNHANES III publishes SAS transport files, which read like continuous NHANES. NHANES I and II publish fixed-width text, which needs the column layouts from CDC's SAS input statements, so historical_file hands back a path to parse rather than a DataFrame.","title":"Historical surveys"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#API-reference","page":"API reference","text":"Nothing is exported, so every name below is reached as NHANES.name. This page is the supported surface. Anything absent from it is an implementation detail, documented under Internals.\n\nPages = [\"api.md\"]","title":"API reference"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#NHANES.DownloadError","page":"API reference","text":"DownloadError <: NHANESError\n\nThrown when downloading data from CDC fails.\n\nFields\n\nurl::String: The URL that failed\nmessage::String: Descriptive error message\nstatus::Union{Int,Nothing}: HTTP status code if available\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.DownloadError"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#NHANES.MetadataError","page":"API reference","text":"MetadataError <: NHANESError\n\nThrown when parsing metadata (codebooks, variable lists) fails.\n\nFields\n\nsource::String: The metadata source (e.g., \"codebook\", \"variable_list\")\nmessage::String: Descriptive error message\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.MetadataError"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#NHANES.NHANESError","page":"API reference","text":"NHANESError <: Exception\n\nBase exception type for all NHANES package errors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.NHANESError"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#NHANES.TableNotFoundError","page":"API reference","text":"TableNotFoundError <: NHANESError\n\nThrown when a requested NHANES table does not exist.\n\nFields\n\ntable::String: The requested table name\nmessage::String: Descriptive error message\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.TableNotFoundError"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.clear_cache-Tuple{}","page":"API reference","text":"clear_cache()\n\nRemove all cached data and metadata.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.clear_cache"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.codebook-Tuple{AbstractString, Symbol}","page":"API reference","text":"codebook(table::AbstractString, variable::Symbol; force::Bool=false) -> DataFrame\n\nGet the codebook (value codes and labels) for a variable.\n\nCodes and labels come from the CDC codebook page, one row per row CDC publishes. Counts are computed from the data, so a continuous variable reports how many observations fall in its published range rather than one row per distinct measurement.\n\nArguments\n\ntable::AbstractString: Table name with suffix (e.g., \"DEMO_J\")\nvariable::Symbol: Variable name (e.g., :RIAGENDR)\nforce::Bool=false: Force refresh from CDC (ignore cache)\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: Value codes with columns:\ncode::String: Code exactly as CDC publishes it, \".\" for missing\nlabel::String: Human-readable label\ncount::Int: Number of observations in the data\n\nExamples\n\n# Get gender codes from 2017-2018 Demographics\nNHANES.codebook(\"DEMO_J\", :RIAGENDR)\n# code | label   | count\n# \"1\"  | Male    | 4557\n# \"2\"  | Female  | 4697\n# \".\"  | Missing | 0\n\n# A continuous variable reports its range, not every observed value\nNHANES.codebook(\"BMX_J\", :BMXWT)\n# code           | label           | count\n# \"3.2 to 242.6\" | Range of Values | 8580\n# \".\"            | Missing         | 124\n\nSee Also\n\nvariables: List all variables in a table\ntranslate!: Apply codebook labels to a DataFrame\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.codebook"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.download-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"download(table::AbstractString; translate::Bool=true, force::Bool=false) -> DataFrame\n\nDownload an NHANES data table and return it as a DataFrame.\n\nTranslation applies to categorical variables only. A variable whose codebook publishes a range of values is a measurement, so its column keeps its numeric element type and its coded missing values (7777 \"Refused\", 9999 \"Don't know\" and friends) stay numeric. Call codebook to find out which numbers a continuous variable reserves for those meanings, and filter them out before analysis.\n\nArguments\n\ntable::AbstractString: Table name with suffix (e.g., \"DEMO_J\" for 2017-2018 Demographics)\ntranslate::Bool=true: Translate coded values to human-readable labels\nforce::Bool=false: If true, re-download even if cached\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: The requested data table\n\nThrows\n\nTableNotFoundError: If CDC has no such table\nDownloadError: If the download fails for any other reason\n\nExamples\n\n# Download 2017-2018 Demographics\ndemo = NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\")\n\n# Download without value translation\ndemo = NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\"; translate=false)\n\nSee Also\n\ntables: List available tables for a component and year\nvariables: List variables in a table\ncodebook: Codes and labels for a single variable\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.download"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.dxa-Tuple{Int64}","page":"API reference","text":"dxa(year::Int; suppl::Bool=false, force::Bool=false) -> DataFrame\n\nDownload DXA data for a survey cycle.\n\nNote: DXA data contains 5 sets of imputed values per participant. Analyze all 5 sets separately - do NOT average them.\n\nArguments\n\nyear::Int: Start year (1999, 2001, 2003, or 2005)\nsuppl::Bool=false: If true, download supplemental data (highly variable imputation)\nforce::Bool=false: Force re-download even if cached\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: DXA measurements with 5 imputation sets\n\nExamples\n\ndxa_data = NHANES.dxa(2005)\ndxa_suppl = NHANES.dxa(2005; suppl=true)\n\nThrows\n\nArgumentError: If the year has no DXA data\nTableNotFoundError: If CDC has no file for the table\nDownloadError: If the download fails for any other reason\n\nSee Also\n\ndxa_tables: List available DXA tables\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.dxa"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.dxa_tables-Tuple{Int64}","page":"API reference","text":"dxa_tables(year::Int; suppl::Bool=false) -> DataFrame\n\nList available DXA tables for a survey cycle.\n\nArguments\n\nyear::Int: Start year (1999, 2001, 2003, or 2005)\nsuppl::Bool=false: If true, list supplemental tables (highly variable imputation data)\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: Available DXA tables with columns: name, description, url\n\nExamples\n\nNHANES.dxa_tables(2005)\nNHANES.dxa_tables(2005; suppl=true)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.dxa_tables"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.historical_download-Tuple{Symbol, AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"historical_download(survey::Symbol, name::AbstractString; force::Bool=false) -> DataFrame\n\nDownload a historical NHANES SAS transport file and return it as a DataFrame.\n\nname is resolved against the historical_tables listing for survey. Only transport files (.xpt) can be read this way, which in practice means NHANES III. NHANES I and II publish fixed-width text whose column layout lives in a separate SAS input statement, so fetch those with historical_file and parse them yourself.\n\nCodes are left as published. Historical surveys have no codebook pages of the kind translate reads.\n\nArguments\n\nsurvey::Symbol: One of :nhanes1, :nhanes2, :nhanes3\nname::AbstractString: File name as reported by historical_tables\nforce::Bool=false: If true, re-download even if cached\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: The requested data file\n\nThrows\n\nArgumentError: If the survey is unknown, or the file is not a transport file\nTableNotFoundError: If the listing holds no file of that name\nDownloadError: If the download fails\n\nExamples\n\nNHANES.historical_download(:nhanes3, \"SSNH3MGM\")\n\nSee Also\n\nhistorical_tables: List the files a survey publishes\nhistorical_file: Download any listed file and return its path\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.historical_download"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.historical_file-Tuple{Symbol, AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"historical_file(survey::Symbol, name::AbstractString; force::Bool=false) -> String\n\nDownload a historical NHANES data file into the cache and return its path.\n\nHandles every file historical_tables lists, whatever its format. Use it for the fixed-width text of NHANES I and II: reading those needs the column layout from the SAS input statement CDC publishes beside the data, which this package does not carry.\n\nArguments\n\nsurvey::Symbol: One of :nhanes1, :nhanes2, :nhanes3\nname::AbstractString: File name as reported by historical_tables\nforce::Bool=false: If true, re-download even if cached\n\nReturns\n\nString: Path to the cached file, under the extension CDC publishes\n\nThrows\n\nArgumentError: If the survey is not one of the historical surveys\nTableNotFoundError: If the listing holds no file of that name\nDownloadError: If the download fails\n\nExamples\n\npath = NHANES.historical_file(:nhanes1, \"DU4111\")\n\nSee Also\n\nhistorical_tables: List the files a survey publishes\nhistorical_download: Read a transport file into a DataFrame\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.historical_file"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.historical_tables-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"API reference","text":"historical_tables(survey::Symbol; force::Bool=false) -> DataFrame\n\nList available data files for a historical NHANES survey.\n\nArguments\n\nsurvey::Symbol: One of :nhanes1, :nhanes2, :nhanes3\nforce::Bool=false: Force refresh from CDC (ignore cache)\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: Available data files with columns: name, description, url\n\nExamples\n\nNHANES.historical_tables(:nhanes3)\n\nThrows\n\nArgumentError: If the survey is not one of the historical surveys\nDownloadError: If the listing page cannot be fetched\n\nNote\n\nHistorical survey data has different structure than continuous NHANES, so download does not handle it. Fetch a listed file with historical_download for the SAS transport files NHANES III publishes, or historical_file for the fixed-width text files of NHANES I and II.\n\nSee Also\n\nhistorical_download: Read a listed transport file into a DataFrame\nhistorical_file: Download any listed file and return its path\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.historical_tables"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.search-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"search(pattern::AbstractString; component::Union{Symbol,Nothing}=nothing,\n       years::Union{Int,AbstractRange,Nothing}=nothing,\n       force::Bool=false) -> DataFrame\n\nSearch for variables matching a pattern across NHANES tables.\n\nEach component and cycle needs one variable list page from CDC, and those pages run to several hundred kilobytes. An unfiltered search fetches one per combination, around 60 pages, SEARCH_CONCURRENCY at a time. Results are cached, so later calls are fast. Narrow the search with component and years to fetch fewer pages.\n\nArguments\n\npattern::AbstractString: Regex pattern to match variable names or descriptions\ncomponent::Union{Symbol,Nothing}=nothing: Filter to specific component\nyears::Union{Int,AbstractRange,Nothing}=nothing: Filter to specific survey cycles\nforce::Bool=false: Force refresh from CDC (ignore cached variable lists)\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: Matching variables with columns:\nvariable: Variable name\ndescription: Variable description\ntable: Table containing the variable\ncomponent: Component type\ncycle: Survey cycle start year, or :P for pre-pandemic\n\nExamples\n\n# Search for blood pressure variables\nNHANES.search(\"blood pressure\")\n\n# Search in Laboratory component only\nNHANES.search(\"glucose\"; component=:Laboratory)\n\n# Search in specific years\nNHANES.search(\"BMI\"; years=2015:2018)\n\nSee Also\n\nvariables: List variables in a specific table\ntables: List available tables\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.search"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.search_table_names-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"search_table_names(pattern::AbstractString;\n                   component::Union{Symbol,Nothing}=nothing,\n                   years::Union{Int,AbstractRange,Nothing}=nothing,\n                   force::Bool=false) -> DataFrame\n\nSearch for tables by name pattern.\n\nTable lists come from the same CDC pages as search, so the same fetching cost applies.\n\nArguments\n\npattern::AbstractString: Regex pattern to match table names\ncomponent::Union{Symbol,Nothing}=nothing: Filter to specific component\nyears::Union{Int,AbstractRange,Nothing}=nothing: Filter to specific survey cycles\nforce::Bool=false: Force refresh from CDC (ignore cached table lists)\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: Matching tables with columns:\nname: Table name\ndescription: Table description\ncomponent: Component type\ncycle: Survey cycle start year, or :P for pre-pandemic\n\nExamples\n\n# Find all BMX tables\nNHANES.search_table_names(\"BMX\")\n\n# Find tables in Laboratory component\nNHANES.search_table_names(\"GLU\"; component=:Laboratory)\n\nSee Also\n\nsearch: Search variables by pattern\nsearch_var_name: Search by exact variable name\ntables: List tables for a component/year\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.search_table_names"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.search_var_name-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"search_var_name(varname::AbstractString;\n                years::Union{Int,AbstractRange,Nothing}=nothing,\n                force::Bool=false) -> DataFrame\n\nSearch for a specific variable name across all NHANES tables.\n\nSearches every component, so the same fetching cost as search applies.\n\nArguments\n\nvarname::AbstractString: Exact variable name to search for (case-insensitive)\nyears::Union{Int,AbstractRange,Nothing}=nothing: Filter to specific survey cycles\nforce::Bool=false: Force refresh from CDC (ignore cached variable lists)\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: Tables containing the variable with columns:\nvariable: Variable name\ntable: Table name\ncomponent: Component type\ncycle: Survey cycle start year, or :P for pre-pandemic\n\nExamples\n\n# Find all tables containing BMXLEG variable\nNHANES.search_var_name(\"BMXLEG\")\n\n# Search in specific years\nNHANES.search_var_name(\"BPXPULS\"; years=2005:2010)\n\nSee Also\n\nsearch: Search by pattern in names and descriptions\nsearch_table_names: Search table names by pattern\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.search_var_name"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.tables-Tuple{Symbol, Union{Int64, Symbol}}","page":"API reference","text":"tables(component::Symbol, year::Union{Int,Symbol}; force::Bool=false) -> DataFrame\n\nList available data tables for a component and survey cycle.\n\nArguments\n\ncomponent::Symbol: One of :Demographics, :Dietary, :Examination, :Laboratory, :Questionnaire\nyear::Union{Int,Symbol}: Start year of the survey cycle (e.g., 2017), or :P for pre-pandemic\nforce::Bool=false: Force refresh from CDC (ignore cache)\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: Available tables with columns:\nname: Table name (e.g., \"DEMOJ\", \"PBMX\")\ndescription: Table description\n\nExamples\n\n# List all laboratory tables for 2017-2018\nNHANES.tables(:Laboratory, 2017)\n\n# List demographics tables for 2015-2016\nNHANES.tables(:Demographics, 2015)\n\n# List pre-pandemic examination tables (2017-March 2020)\nNHANES.tables(:Examination, :P)\n\nSee Also\n\ndownload: Download a specific table\nvariables: List variables in a table\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.tables"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.translate!-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame, AbstractString, Symbol}","page":"API reference","text":"translate!(df::DataFrame, table::AbstractString, column::Symbol)\n\nReplace numeric codes with text labels in-place.\n\nOnly the codebook labels are fetched, so translating several columns reads the data table once.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: DataFrame to modify\ntable::AbstractString: Table name (for looking up codebook)\ncolumn::Symbol: Column to translate\n\nThrows\n\nMetadataError: If the codebook does not describe the column\nArgumentError: If the column holds measurements rather than codes\n\nExamples\n\ndemo = NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\"; translate=false)\nNHANES.translate!(demo, \"DEMO_J\", :RIAGENDR)\n# Column now contains \"Male\"/\"Female\" instead of 1/2\n\nSee Also\n\ntranslate: Non-mutating version\ncodebook: View available codes\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.translate!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.translate!-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame, AbstractString, Vector{Symbol}}","page":"API reference","text":"translate!(df::DataFrame, table::AbstractString, columns::Vector{Symbol})\n\nTranslate multiple columns in-place.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.translate!"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.translate-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame, AbstractString, Symbol}","page":"API reference","text":"translate(df::DataFrame, table::AbstractString, column::Symbol) -> DataFrame\ntranslate(df::DataFrame, table::AbstractString, columns::Vector{Symbol}) -> DataFrame\n\nReturn a new DataFrame with codes replaced by labels.\n\nNon-mutating version of translate!.\n\nArguments\n\ndf::DataFrame: Source DataFrame\ntable::AbstractString: Table name (for looking up codebook)\ncolumn::Symbol or columns::Vector{Symbol}: Column(s) to translate\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: New DataFrame with translated column(s)\n\nExamples\n\ndemo = NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\"; translate=false)\ndemo_labeled = NHANES.translate(demo, \"DEMO_J\", :RIAGENDR)\ndemo_labeled = NHANES.translate(demo, \"DEMO_J\", [:RIAGENDR, :RIDRETH1])\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.translate"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#NHANES.variables-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"API reference","text":"variables(table::AbstractString; force::Bool=false) -> DataFrame\n\nList variables in an NHANES data table.\n\nArguments\n\ntable::AbstractString: Table name with suffix (e.g., \"DEMO_J\")\nforce::Bool=false: Force refresh from CDC (ignore cache)\n\nReturns\n\nDataFrame: Variables with columns:\nname: Variable name\nlabel: Variable description/label\n\nExamples\n\n# List variables in 2017-2018 Demographics\nNHANES.variables(\"DEMO_J\")\n\nSee Also\n\ncodebook: Get value codes for a variable\ndownload: Download the table data\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.variables"},{"category":"section","location":"nhanesa/#Coming-from-nhanesA","page":"Coming from nhanesA","text":"R's nhanesA covers the same data. The call names map across directly.\n\nnhanesA (R) NHANES.jl\nnhanes(\"DEMO_J\") NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\")\nnhanes(\"DEMO_J\", translate=FALSE) NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\"; translate=false)\nnhanesTables(\"EXAM\", 2005) NHANES.tables(:EXAM, 2005)\nnhanesTableVars(\"EXAM\", \"BMX_D\") NHANES.variables(\"BMX_D\")\nnhanesCodebook(\"DEMO_D\", \"RIAGENDR\") NHANES.codebook(\"DEMO_D\", :RIAGENDR)\nnhanesTranslate(\"BPX_D\", \"BPXSY1\", data=df) NHANES.translate!(df, \"BPX_D\", :BPXSY1)\nnhanesSearch(\"glucose\") NHANES.search(\"glucose\")\nnhanesSearchVarName(\"BMXLEG\") NHANES.search_var_name(\"BMXLEG\")\nnhanesSearchTableNames(\"BMX\") NHANES.search_table_names(\"BMX\")\nnhanesDXA(2005) NHANES.dxa(2005)\nnhanesDXA(2005, suppl=TRUE) NHANES.dxa(2005; suppl=true)","title":"Coming from nhanesA"},{"category":"section","location":"nhanesa/#Where-the-two-differ","page":"Coming from nhanesA","text":"Both translate coded values by default, but they disagree on continuous variables. nhanesA converts a column to character as soon as the codebook reserves any code, so age, income ratio and the survey weights come back as strings. NHANES.jl leaves those columns numeric and skips translation for them, which means a weighted analysis works on the frame as returned.\n\nThe cost is that reserved codes stay in the column as numbers. See Value translation for how to find and filter them.\n\nComponent names accept the R short forms:\n\n:DEMO or :Demographics\n:DIET or :Dietary\n:EXAM or :Examination\n:LAB or :Laboratory\n:Q or :Questionnaire","title":"Where the two differ"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Guide","page":"Guide","text":"Every call on this page fetches from wwwn.cdc.gov. The documentation build does not run them, so results are described rather than shown.","title":"Guide"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Downloading-data","page":"Guide","text":"download takes a table name and returns a DataFrame.\n\ndf = NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\")                      # translated, cached\ndf = NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\"; translate = false)   # numeric codes\ndf = NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\"; force = true)        # ignore the cache\n\nAn unknown name raises NHANES.TableNotFoundError, because CDC answers 404 for one. See Survey cycles and table names for how a year and a component map onto a name.","title":"Downloading data"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Listing-tables-and-variables","page":"Guide","text":"NHANES.tables(:Demographics, 2017)   # tables published for 2017-2018\nNHANES.tables(:Examination, :P)      # the 2017-March 2020 pre-pandemic cycle\nNHANES.variables(\"DEMO_J\")           # variable names and labels in one table\n\nComponents are :Demographics, :Dietary, :Examination, :Laboratory and :Questionnaire. The R-style short forms :DEMO, :DIET, :EXAM, :LAB and :Q work too, in any case.\n\nSome tables a listing reports are marked \"RDC Only\", meaning access is restricted to a Research Data Center. Those cannot be downloaded.","title":"Listing tables and variables"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Codebooks","page":"Guide","text":"codebook reports the codes CDC publishes for a variable, with counts taken from the data.\n\nNHANES.codebook(\"DEMO_J\", :RIAGENDR)\n# 3×3 DataFrame\n#  Row │ code    label    count\n#      │ String  String   Int64\n# ─────┼────────────────────────\n#    1 │ 1       Male      4557\n#    2 │ 2       Female    4697\n#    3 │ .       Missing      0\n\ncode is a String carrying the code exactly as published, so a continuous variable reports its range rather than one row per observed value.\n\nNHANES.codebook(\"BMX_J\", :BMXWT)\n# 2×3 DataFrame\n#  Row │ code          label            count\n#      │ String        String           Int64\n# ─────┼──────────────────────────────────────\n#    1 │ 3.2 to 242.6  Range of Values   8580\n#    2 │ .             Missing            124","title":"Codebooks"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Value-translation","page":"Guide","text":"download translates categorical variables to their labels and leaves continuous variables numeric. RIAGENDR comes back as \"Male\" or \"Female\", while RIDAGEYR and the survey weight WTMEC2YR stay Float64.\n\nReserved codes on a continuous variable (7 or 7777 for \"Refused\", 9 or 9999 for \"Don't know\", and similar) stay numeric with the rest of the column, so an unguarded mean includes them. Call codebook to see which codes a variable reserves, and filter them before summarising.\n\ndemo = NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\"; translate = false)\nNHANES.translate!(demo, \"DEMO_J\", :RIAGENDR)\nNHANES.translate!(demo, \"DEMO_J\", [:RIAGENDR, :RIDRETH1])\n\nlabelled = NHANES.translate(demo, \"DEMO_J\", :RIAGENDR)   # leaves demo alone\n\nTranslating a continuous variable raises ArgumentError rather than producing a column of stringified numbers.","title":"Value translation"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Searching","page":"Guide","text":"NHANES.search(\"glucose\")\nNHANES.search(\"cholesterol\"; component = :Laboratory)\nNHANES.search(\"BMI\"; years = 2015:2018)\n\nNHANES.search_var_name(\"BMXLEG\")            # exact variable name\nNHANES.search_table_names(\"BMX\")            # table name pattern\n\nNHANES.search(\"glucose\"; force = true)      # refresh the cached lists\n\nAn unfiltered search covers every component and cycle, about 60 pages. They are fetched six at a time, so a cold call takes roughly ten seconds; later calls read the 30-day metadata cache and return in a fraction of a second. Narrowing with component or years cuts the first call down.","title":"Searching"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#DXA","page":"Guide","text":"Dual-energy X-ray absorptiometry data covers 1999-2006 and is published apart from the main tables.\n\nNHANES.dxa_tables(2005)\nNHANES.dxa(2005)\nNHANES.dxa(2005; suppl = true)   # highly variable imputation data\n\nEach DXA dataset carries five imputation sets per participant. Analyse the five separately. Averaging them understates the variance the imputation exists to represent.","title":"DXA"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Historical-surveys","page":"Guide","text":"The surveys before continuous NHANES publish files rather than the tables download reads.\n\nNHANES.historical_tables(:nhanes1)   # 1971-1975\nNHANES.historical_tables(:nhanes2)   # 1976-1980\nNHANES.historical_tables(:nhanes3)   # 1988-1994\n\nEach row carries a name, a description and an absolute url. NHANES III publishes SAS transport files, which read like continuous NHANES:\n\ndf = NHANES.historical_download(:nhanes3, \"SSNH3MGM\")\n\nNHANES I and II publish fixed-width text. Reading it needs the column layout from the SAS input statement CDC ships beside the data, which this package does not carry, so historical_file downloads the file and hands back its path:\n\npath = NHANES.historical_file(:nhanes1, \"DU4111\")\n\nhistorical_download rejects a fixed-width file rather than guessing at its layout. historical_file accepts anything a listing reports, transport files included.","title":"Historical surveys"},{"category":"section","location":"guide/#Caching","page":"Guide","text":"XPT files are cached permanently, since published NHANES data does not change. Scraped metadata expires after 30 days. Both live under ~/.julia/scratchspaces/.\n\nNHANES.clear_cache()","title":"Caching"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/#Internals","page":"Internals","text":"Everything the API reference does not list, including names without a leading underscore. None of it carries a compatibility guarantee.\n\nThe two filters partition the module and checkdocs = :all fails the build on any docstring that falls through both, so a name added to one list and not removed from the other cannot slip past CI.","title":"Internals"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._all_cycles-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"All cycles to search by default (regular years + pre-pandemic).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._all_cycles"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._apply_labels!-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_apply_labels!(df::DataFrames.DataFrame, table::AbstractString)\n\nApply value labels to the categorical columns of a DataFrame. Continuous columns keep their numeric values. Uses cached labels, no redundant downloads.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._apply_labels!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._build_codebook_from_data-Tuple{DataFrames.DataFrame, Symbol, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_build_codebook_from_data(df::DataFrames.DataFrame, variable::Symbol, entry) -> DataFrame\n\nBuild codebook DataFrame with counts computed from actual data.\n\nEmits one row per row CDC publishes, in order. Values matching no published code are appended so the counts account for every observation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._build_codebook_from_data"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._code_sort_key-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_code_sort_key(code::AbstractString)\n\nSort key placing numeric codes in numeric order ahead of non-numeric ones.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._code_sort_key"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._directory-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"Directory part of a URL path, including the trailing slash.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._directory"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._dxa_table_name-Tuple{Int64, Bool}","page":"Internals","text":"Build DXA table name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._dxa_table_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._dxa_url-Tuple{Int64, Bool}","page":"Internals","text":"Build URL for DXA data file.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._dxa_url"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._fetch_pages-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_fetch_pages(f, components, cycles) -> Vector{Tuple}\n\nApply f(component, cycle) to every pair, keeping up to SEARCH_CONCURRENCY fetches in flight, and return (component, cycle, result) triples in components by cycles order however the fetches interleave. Pairs CDC does not publish are dropped, as in _skip_missing. A failure surfaces with its original type once the fetches in flight settle, and stops the remaining pairs from being fetched.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._fetch_pages"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._format_code-Tuple{Real}","page":"Internals","text":"Format numeric code for label lookup.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._format_code"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._get_cached_variablelist-Tuple{Symbol, Union{Int64, Symbol}}","page":"Internals","text":"_get_cached_variablelist(component::Symbol, year::Union{Int,Symbol};\n                         force::Bool=false) -> Vector{Dict}\n\nGet variable list for a component/year, using cache if available.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._get_cached_variablelist"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._get_table_labels-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_get_table_labels(table::AbstractString; force::Bool=false) -> Dict\n\nGet the parsed value table for every variable in a data table, using cache if available. Returns Dict mapping variable name -> value table, as built by _parse_all_value_labels.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._get_table_labels"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._historical_cache_path-Tuple{Symbol, AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_historical_cache_path(survey::Symbol, name::AbstractString, extension::AbstractString) -> String\n\nCache file path for a historical data file, keeping the extension CDC publishes it under.\n\nThrows\n\nArgumentError: If the name is not a plain identifier, or the extension is not one CDC publishes data under\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._historical_cache_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._historical_entry-Tuple{Symbol, DataFrames.DataFrame, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_historical_entry(survey::Symbol, listing::DataFrames.DataFrame, name::AbstractString) -> NamedTuple\n\nFind name in a survey listing, reporting its name, URL and file extension. Lookup ignores case because listing names are always uppercase.\n\nThrows\n\nTableNotFoundError: If the listing holds no file of that name\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._historical_entry"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._historical_fetch-Tuple{Symbol, NamedTuple}","page":"Internals","text":"Path of the cached copy of entry, downloading it first when needed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._historical_fetch"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._historical_tables_url-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"_historical_tables_url(survey::Symbol) -> String\n\nGet URL for historical survey tables list. NHANES I/II use default.aspx, NHANES III uses datafiles.aspx.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._historical_tables_url"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._is_blank-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_is_blank(val) -> Bool\n\nReport whether a data value is absent. A character column records a blank string where a numeric column records missing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._is_blank"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._is_historical_data_file-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_is_historical_data_file(filename::AbstractString) -> Bool\n\nReport whether a linked file holds survey data. Readme files sit next to the data files and share their extension, so they are excluded by name.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._is_historical_data_file"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._is_missing_row-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_is_missing_row(code::AbstractString) -> Bool\n\nReport whether a value table row counts missing observations rather than a code.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._is_missing_row"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._is_range_row-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_is_range_row(code::AbstractString, label::AbstractString) -> Bool\n\nReport whether a value table row describes a range of measurements rather than a single code. CDC marks these rows with the description \"Range of Values\" and a code cell such as \"3.2 to 242.6\". A character variable's recorded values are also ranges: their code cell repeats the variable description.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._is_range_row"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._normalize_path-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"Collapse . and .. segments in an absolute URL path.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._normalize_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._parse_all_value_labels-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_parse_all_value_labels(html::AbstractString) -> Dict{String,Any}\n\nParse the value table of every variable on a codebook page.\n\nReturns Dict mapping variable name -> Dict with:\n\n\"continuous\": true when the variable has a range row, so its values are measurements rather than codes\n\"labels\": Dict(code_string -> label) for code rows only\n\"rows\": every published row, in order, as Dict(\"code\" =>, \"label\" =>)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._parse_all_value_labels"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._parse_historical_tables-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_parse_historical_tables(html::AbstractString, page_url::AbstractString) -> Vector{Dict}\n\nParse a historical survey listing page. Names are derived from the data file names, which are more reliable than the surrounding description cells. Links are resolved against page_url.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._parse_historical_tables"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._parse_tables_from_variablelist-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_parse_tables_from_variablelist(html::AbstractString) -> Vector{Dict}\n\nExtract unique table information from a variable list page. Each variable on the page names the data file it belongs to.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._parse_tables_from_variablelist"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._parse_variables_from_codebook-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"_parse_variables_from_codebook(html::AbstractString) -> Vector{Dict}\n\nExtract variable names and labels from a codebook page.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._parse_variables_from_codebook"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._require_transport_file-Tuple{NamedTuple}","page":"Internals","text":"Reject a listing entry that historical_download cannot read.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._require_transport_file"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._search_components-Tuple{Union{Nothing, Symbol}}","page":"Internals","text":"_search_components(component::Union{Symbol,Nothing}) -> Vector{Symbol}\n\nComponents a search covers: every component, or just the one requested.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._search_components"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._search_cycles-Tuple{Union{Nothing, Int64, AbstractRange}}","page":"Internals","text":"_search_cycles(years::Union{Int,AbstractRange,Nothing}) -> Vector{Union{Int,Symbol}}\n\nCycles a search covers, in survey order, dropping years CDC has not published.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._search_cycles"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._search_results_to_dataframe-Tuple{Vector}","page":"Internals","text":"_search_results_to_dataframe(results::Vector) -> DataFrame\n\nConvert search results to a DataFrame.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._search_results_to_dataframe"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._skip_missing-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_skip_missing(f)\n\nRun f, returning nothing when CDC publishes no page for the request. Every other failure propagates, so a network outage or a markup change is not mistaken for an empty result.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._skip_missing"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._split_path-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"Split a URL path from the query string or fragment that follows it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._split_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._tables_to_dataframe-Tuple{Vector}","page":"Internals","text":"_tables_to_dataframe(data::Vector) -> DataFrame\n\nConvert parsed tables data to a DataFrame. Includes URL column if present in data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._tables_to_dataframe"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._translate_column-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_translate_column(col, labels_map) -> (Vector{Union{String,Missing}}, Set{String})\n\nReplace codes with labels, keeping unlabelled values as strings. Returns the translated column and the codes that had no label.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._translate_column"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._variables_to_dataframe-Tuple{Vector}","page":"Internals","text":"_variables_to_dataframe(data::Vector) -> DataFrame\n\nConvert parsed variables data to a DataFrame.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._variables_to_dataframe"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES._warn_unmatched-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"_warn_unmatched(table::AbstractString, column::AbstractString, codes)\n\nReport codes present in the data that the codebook does not describe.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES._warn_unmatched"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.cache_dir-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"cache_dir() -> String\n\nGet the root cache directory for NHANES data. Creates the directory if it doesn't exist.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.cache_dir"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.codebook_url-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"codebook_url(table::AbstractString) -> String\n\nBuild the URL for a table's codebook/documentation page.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.codebook_url"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.cycle_suffix-Tuple{Int64}","page":"Internals","text":"cycle_suffix(year::Int) -> String\n\nGet the table suffix for a given survey cycle start year.\n\nThrows\n\nArgumentError: If the year is not a published cycle. 2019 gets a dedicated message pointing at the pre-pandemic cycle :P.\n\nExamples\n\ncycle_suffix(1999)  # \"\"\ncycle_suffix(2017)  # \"_J\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.cycle_suffix"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.data_cache_path-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"data_cache_path(table::AbstractString) -> String\n\nGet the cache file path for a data table.\n\nThrows\n\nArgumentError: If the table name is not a plain identifier\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.data_cache_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.extract_text-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internals","text":"extract_text(node) -> String\n\nConcatenate the text content of an HTML node and its descendants.\n\nText nodes are joined without a separator, so inline markup inside a cell does not introduce whitespace that the rendered page does not have.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.extract_text"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.fetch_file-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"fetch_file(url::AbstractString, dest::AbstractString; retries::Int=3) -> String\n\nDownload a file from a URL to a destination path.\n\nThe transfer goes to a temporary file next to dest and is renamed into place once complete, so a failed download never leaves a truncated file at dest.\n\nArguments\n\nurl::AbstractString: URL to download from\ndest::AbstractString: Local path to save the file\nretries::Int=3: Maximum number of attempts\n\nThrows\n\nDownloadError: If the download fails\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.fetch_file"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.fetch_html-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"fetch_html(url::AbstractString; retries::Int=3) -> String\n\nFetch HTML content from a URL.\n\nArguments\n\nurl::AbstractString: URL to fetch\nretries::Int=3: Maximum number of attempts\n\nThrows\n\nDownloadError: If the fetch fails\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.fetch_html"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.http_status-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internals","text":"http_status(e) -> Union{Int,Nothing}\n\nGet the HTTP status carried by a failure, or nothing when the request failed before a response arrived.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.http_status"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.is_cached-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"is_cached(table::AbstractString) -> Bool\n\nCheck if a data table is cached.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.is_cached"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.is_metadata_fresh-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"is_metadata_fresh(path::AbstractString) -> Bool\n\nCheck if a metadata cache file exists and is within the TTL.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.is_metadata_fresh"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.is_transient-Tuple{Any}","page":"Internals","text":"is_transient(e) -> Bool\n\nReport whether a failure is worth retrying: connection and timeout failures, HTTP 429, and HTTP 5xx. A 4xx response means the resource will not appear on a second attempt.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.is_transient"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.load_metadata-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"load_metadata(category::AbstractString, key::AbstractString)\n\nLoad metadata from the cache.\n\nReturns\n\nParsed JSON data, or nothing if not cached or stale\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.load_metadata"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.metadata_cache_path-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"metadata_cache_path(category::AbstractString, key::AbstractString) -> String\n\nGet the cache file path for metadata.\n\nThrows\n\nArgumentError: If the category or key is not a plain identifier\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.metadata_cache_path"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.normalize_component-Tuple{Symbol}","page":"Internals","text":"normalize_component(comp::Symbol) -> Symbol\n\nConvert a component name to its full form. Accepts full names and R-style short names (:DEMO, :DIET, :EXAM, :LAB, :Q), both case-insensitive. Returns: :Demographics, :Dietary, :Examination, :Laboratory, :Questionnaire\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.normalize_component"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.parse_table_name-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"parse_table_name(table::AbstractString) -> Tuple{String, String}\n\nParse a table name into its base name and cycle marker.\n\nReturns\n\nTuple{String, String}: (basename, cyclemarker)\nFor suffix tables: (\"DEMO\", \"_J\")\nFor P_ prefix tables: (\"BMX\", \"P_\")\nFor 1999-2000 tables: (\"DEMO\", \"\")\n\nExamples\n\nparse_table_name(\"DEMO_J\")    # (\"DEMO\", \"_J\")\nparse_table_name(\"ALB_CR_J\")  # (\"ALB_CR\", \"_J\")\nparse_table_name(\"P_BMX\")     # (\"BMX\", \"P_\")\nparse_table_name(\"DEMO\")      # (\"DEMO\", \"\")\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.parse_table_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.parse_variablelist_html-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"parse_variablelist_html(html::AbstractString) -> Vector{Dict}\n\nParse a variable list HTML page.\n\nReturns\n\nVector{Dict}: One entry per variable, with name, description, table and table_description keys\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.parse_variablelist_html"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.resolve_url-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"resolve_url(base::AbstractString, href::AbstractString) -> String\n\nResolve a link against the absolute URL of the page it appeared on.\n\nAbsolute links are returned unchanged and protocol-relative links take the scheme of base. Everything else is joined onto base, with . and .. segments collapsed and .. stopping at the root.\n\nThrows\n\nArgumentError: If base is not an absolute URL\n\nExamples\n\nresolve_url(\n    \"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/nchs/nhanes/nhanes3/datafiles.aspx\",\n    \"../../data/nhanes3/1a/adult.dat\",\n)\n# \"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/nchs/data/nhanes3/1a/adult.dat\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.resolve_url"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.save_metadata-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString, Any}","page":"Internals","text":"save_metadata(category::AbstractString, key::AbstractString, data) -> String\n\nSave metadata to the cache as JSON.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.save_metadata"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.suffix_to_year-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"suffix_to_year(suffix::AbstractString) -> Int\n\nConvert a table suffix to the survey cycle start year. The leading underscore is optional.\n\nExamples\n\nsuffix_to_year(\"_J\")  # 2017\nsuffix_to_year(\"B\")   # 2001\nsuffix_to_year(\"\")    # 1999\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.suffix_to_year"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.survey_years-Tuple{}","page":"Internals","text":"survey_years() -> Vector{Int}\n\nList the start years of every published survey cycle, in ascending order.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.survey_years"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.table_rows-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"table_rows(html::AbstractString) -> Vector{Vector{String}}\n\nExtract the text of the td cells of every table row on a page, one entry per row. Header rows, which hold th cells, come back empty.\n\nReturns\n\nVector{Vector{String}}: Cell text per row, in document order\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.table_rows"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.table_url-Tuple{AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"table_url(table::AbstractString) -> String\n\nBuild the download URL for an NHANES data table.\n\nExamples\n\ntable_url(\"DEMO_J\")\n# \"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Data/Nhanes/Public/2017/DataFiles/DEMO_J.xpt\"\n\ntable_url(\"P_BMX\")\n# \"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/Nchs/Data/Nhanes/Public/2017/DataFiles/P_BMX.xpt\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.table_url"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.validate_name-Tuple{AbstractString, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"validate_name(name::AbstractString, kind::AbstractString) -> String\n\nCheck that a name cannot escape the directory or URL path it is joined into. Returns the name unchanged.\n\nThrows\n\nArgumentError: If the name contains anything but letters, digits and underscores\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.validate_name"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.variablelist_url-Tuple{Symbol, Union{Int64, Symbol}}","page":"Internals","text":"variablelist_url(component::Symbol, year::Union{Int,Symbol}) -> String\n\nBuild the URL for the variable list page.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.variablelist_url"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.with_cache_dir-Tuple{Any, AbstractString}","page":"Internals","text":"with_cache_dir(f, dir::AbstractString)\n\nRun f with the cache root redirected to dir, restoring the previous root afterwards.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.with_cache_dir"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/#NHANES.with_retries-Tuple{Any, AbstractString, AbstractString, Int64}","page":"Internals","text":"with_retries(f, url, action, retries; backoff = RETRY_BACKOFF_SECONDS)\n\nRun f, retrying transient failures with exponential backoff.\n\nArguments\n\nf: Zero-argument function performing the request\nurl::AbstractString: URL being requested, reported in errors\naction::AbstractString: What f is doing, reported in errors\nretries::Int: Maximum number of attempts\nbackoff::Real: Delay in seconds before the first retry\n\nThrows\n\nDownloadError: If the request fails permanently or runs out of attempts\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.with_retries"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.CACHE_ROOT_OVERRIDE","page":"Internals","text":"Cache root to use instead of the Scratch.jl space, or nothing for the default. Tests redirect the cache here so they never touch a real download cache; see with_cache_dir.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.CACHE_ROOT_OVERRIDE"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.COMPONENTS","page":"Internals","text":"Valid NHANES data components for continuous NHANES (1999-present).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.COMPONENTS"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.COMPONENT_ALIASES","page":"Internals","text":"Mapping from R-style short component names to full names.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.COMPONENT_ALIASES"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.COMPONENT_LOOKUP","page":"Internals","text":"Mapping from lowercased component spellings, both full names and R-style aliases, to full names. Backs case-insensitive lookup.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.COMPONENT_LOOKUP"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.DXA_YEARS","page":"Internals","text":"Valid years for DXA data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.DXA_YEARS"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.HISTORICAL_DATA_EXTENSIONS","page":"Internals","text":"File extensions of the historical data files CDC publishes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.HISTORICAL_DATA_EXTENSIONS"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.HISTORICAL_SURVEYS","page":"Internals","text":"Historical survey identifiers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.HISTORICAL_SURVEYS"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.METADATA_TTL_DAYS","page":"Internals","text":"Number of days before metadata cache is considered stale.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.METADATA_TTL_DAYS"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.MISSING_CODE","page":"Internals","text":"Code cell CDC uses for the missing row of a numeric value table.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.MISSING_CODE"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.MISSING_CODES","page":"Internals","text":"Code cells CDC uses for the missing row, numeric and character.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.MISSING_CODES"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.PREPANDEMIC_CYCLE","page":"Internals","text":"Pre-pandemic cycle identifier (2017-March 2020). Tables use P_ prefix instead of suffix.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.PREPANDEMIC_CYCLE"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.RANGE_DESCRIPTION","page":"Internals","text":"Description CDC uses for the row covering a variable's measured range.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.RANGE_DESCRIPTION"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.RETRY_BACKOFF_SECONDS","page":"Internals","text":"Base delay in seconds before a retry, doubled on each further attempt.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.RETRY_BACKOFF_SECONDS"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.SAFE_NAME","page":"Internals","text":"Names that are safe to embed in a cache path or a CDC URL.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.SAFE_NAME"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.SEARCH_CONCURRENCY","page":"Internals","text":"Number of CDC page fetches allowed in flight at once. Six matches the per-host connection limit browsers use, so a search asks no more of wwwn.cdc.gov than loading the same pages in a browser would, and measured throughput stops improving beyond it.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.SEARCH_CONCURRENCY"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.SUFFIX_TO_YEAR","page":"Internals","text":"Mapping of table suffixes back to survey cycle start years.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.SUFFIX_TO_YEAR"},{"category":"constant","location":"internals/#NHANES.SURVEY_CYCLES","page":"Internals","text":"Mapping of survey cycle start years to table suffixes.\n\nContinuous NHANES uses letter suffixes starting from 1999-2000:\n\n1999-2000: no suffix (or sometimes _A in older tables)\n2001-2002: _B\n2003-2004: _C\netc.\n\nThe 2019-2020 cycle was cut short by COVID-19 and never published on its own. Its data was released as part of the 2017-March 2020 pre-pandemic files, and CDC skipped the letter _K, so 2021-2023 uses _L.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.SURVEY_CYCLES"},{"category":"section","location":"#NHANES.jl","page":"Home","text":"Access CDC NHANES (National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey) data from Julia: download data tables, list what a cycle publishes, read codebooks, and translate coded values to their labels.","title":"NHANES.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Installation","page":"Home","text":"using Pkg\nPkg.add(url = \"https://github.com/PumasAI/NHANES.jl\")","title":"Installation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Nothing-is-exported","page":"Home","text":"Reach every entry point through the module. download, search, tables and translate are names Base and other packages use too, so exporting them would make the package unsafe to combine.\n\nimport NHANES\n\ndemo = NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\")","title":"Nothing is exported"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quick-start","page":"Home","text":"Each call below fetches from wwwn.cdc.gov. The documentation build does not run them, so the results are described rather than shown.\n\nimport NHANES\n\ndemo = NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\")        # 2017-2018 demographics, as a DataFrame\nNHANES.tables(:Laboratory, 2015)        # laboratory tables published for 2015-2016\nNHANES.variables(\"DEMO_J\")              # variable names and labels in a table\nNHANES.codebook(\"DEMO_J\", :RIAGENDR)    # codes, labels and counts for one variable\nNHANES.search(\"blood pressure\")         # variables whose description matches\n\nThe Guide covers each of these in turn. Survey cycles and table names explains how a year maps onto a table name, and the API reference lists the full call surface.","title":"Quick start"},{"category":"section","location":"#Errors","page":"Home","text":"Every failure raises a subtype of NHANES.NHANESError.\n\njulia> err = NHANES.TableNotFoundError(\"DEMO_X\", \"Table not found: DEMO_X\")\nNHANES.TableNotFoundError(\"DEMO_X\", \"Table not found: DEMO_X\")\n\njulia> err isa NHANES.NHANESError\ntrue\n\njulia> sprint(showerror, err)\n\"TableNotFoundError: Table not found: DEMO_X\"\n\nDownloadError carries the HTTP status when there was one.\n\njulia> sprint(showerror, NHANES.DownloadError(\"https://wwwn.cdc.gov/x.xpt\", \"Failed to download\", 503))\n\"DownloadError: Failed to download (HTTP 503)\"\n\njulia> sprint(showerror, NHANES.MetadataError(\"codebook\", \"No value tables found\"))\n\"MetadataError: No value tables found (source: codebook)\"\n\nCDC answers 404 for an unknown table name, which surfaces as TableNotFoundError. Connection failures, 429 and 5xx are retried with exponential backoff before surfacing as DownloadError. Other 4xx responses are not retried.\n\nTable names are checked before they reach a URL or a cache path.\n\njulia> NHANES.table_url(\"../../etc/passwd\")\nERROR: ArgumentError: Invalid table name: \"../../etc/passwd\". Only letters, digits and underscores are allowed.","title":"Errors"},{"category":"module","location":"#NHANES.NHANES","page":"Home","text":"NHANES\n\nJulia package for accessing CDC NHANES (National Health and Nutrition Examination Survey) data.\n\nNothing is exported. Reach everything through the module.\n\nQuick Start\n\nimport NHANES\n\ndemo = NHANES.download(\"DEMO_J\")\nNHANES.tables(:Laboratory, 2017)\nNHANES.search(\"blood pressure\")\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"NHANES.NHANES"}]
}
